{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe downward bias: The model consistently overestimates prices by 5-10 EUR during the initial 10-day horizon following a price drop, failing to anticipate the depth of the correction.",
    "Adjust for excessive lag in mean reversion: The model assumes a slow, linear recovery (or flat trend) after a crash, whereas true outcomes show a sharper V-shaped recovery starting around day 10-12; forecasts must be adjusted downward initially and then accelerated upward.",
    "Incorporate sentiment-triggered volatility: When sentiment history shows a negative spike (-1.00), the model's assumption of stability is invalid; apply an immediate downward correction of 3-5 EUR to the forecast for the next 5 days.",
    "Reduce forecast ceiling: The model projects a steady, monotonic increase to ~64 EUR, but true outcomes cap near 60-61 EUR before stabilizing; cap the long-term forecast at 61.50 EUR to prevent overshooting the actual ceiling.",
    "Account for sentiment lag: Positive sentiment signals (0.20) in the history do not immediately translate to price increases in the model; delay the upward adjustment in the forecast by 3-4 days to align with the actual market reaction time."
  ]
}
